### IPP-303 registration + email verification tests
### How to use: run `npm run dev` in /server, then click "Send Request" above each request, top to bottom.
### Use an email inbox you can open (e.g. your Gmail with +test: yourname+ipp1@gmail.com).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@email = arsalmustafa62+ipp2@gmail.com

### Step 3 needs the token from the email link:
### the link looks like http://localhost:5173/verify-email/<64 characters>
### copy those 64 characters and paste after "@verifyToken = ".
### (The same link is also printed in the server terminal as "[dev] Verify link ...")
@verifyToken = a96ab5a5fb5dcd6f14ce1e9a65440562623912f48954a2720250c31a9a06f5a4


### 1. Register with bad data -> expect 400 with a list of errors
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "email": "abc",
  "password": "1"
}


### 2. Register -> expect 201 "Account created. Please check your email..."
###    data.user.isVerified = false, and NO password / token in the response.
###    Check your inbox (and spam) for the "Verify your email" email.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "secret123"
}


### 3. Verify with the token from the email -> expect 200 "Email verified. You can now log in"
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-email/{{verifyToken}}


### 4. Same link again -> expect 400 "This verification link is invalid or has expired..."
###    (each link works only once)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-email/{{verifyToken}}


### 5. Broken link -> expect 400 "Invalid verification link"
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-email/abc123


### 6. Register the same (now verified) email again -> expect 409 "This email is already registered. Please log in"
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "secret123"
}


### 7. Resend for a verified email -> expect 200 with the general message (no email is sent)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/resend-verification
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}"
}


### 8. Resend for an email that is not registered -> expect the SAME 200 message
###    (so nobody can find out which emails are registered)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/resend-verification
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody-here@example.com"
}


### ---- Resend flow with a second, unverified account ----

### 9. Register a second email -> expect 201 (an email is sent)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Second User",
  "email": "arsalmustafa62+ipp3@gmail.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}


### 10. Resend straight away -> expect 429 "Please wait a minute before asking for another email"
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/resend-verification
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "arsalmustafa62+ipp3@gmail.com"
}


### 11. Wait 1 minute, send again -> expect 200 and a NEW email.
###     The link in the first email for this account now gives 400 (only the newest link works).
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/resend-verification
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "arsalmustafa62+ipp3@gmail.com"
}


### NOTE: register / resend allow 10 emails per hour per IP. If you get 429
### "Too many emails requested", restart `npm run dev` (the counter resets).
### Clean up test users afterwards in Atlas (Browse Collections -> users), or keep them for IPP-304.
